045465 13194139535738 true] [17592186364109 1100 "Solve for $x$ in $Ax=b$ given that the matrix $A$ is orthogonal, and \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364109 1113 #uuid "5d295ce9-f8cd-5701-932f-c89dd90a82fd" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364109 1145 "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nHence, since $A$ is orthogonal, we have ${A}^{-1}={A}^{T}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364111 13194139535738 true] [17592186364110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364112 13194139535738 true] [17592186364110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364113 13194139535738 true] [17592186364110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364114 13194139535738 true] [17592186364110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364115 13194139535738 true] [17592186364110 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535738 true] [17592186364110 1041 "selection" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364110 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364115 13194139535738 true] [17592186364110 1110 #uuid "0f0511d0-8a4e-59ec-9b57-c90432e1d4f1" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364111 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535738 true] [17592186364111 1111 #uuid "aa167f5a-1f46-55bf-9471-be47db88179e" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364112 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535738 true] [17592186364112 1111 #uuid "fe596c4d-6951-5f21-b250-68c5ca9c41ee" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364113 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535738 true] [17592186364113 1111 #uuid "62dc48df-5ee0-5887-a3e4-d4acfb178275" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364114 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535738 true] [17592186364114 1111 #uuid "4a638be6-fb81-5e96-8b36-bdc85cc92b28" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364115 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535738 true] [17592186364115 1111 #uuid "152e673c-783b-5471-8da5-5dd2fb9eddd4" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364117 13194139535738 true] [17592186364116 1089 "q-84347" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364116 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535738 true] [17592186364116 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the orthogonal matrix $P?$\n\n- ${P}^{T}$ is orthogonal\n- ${P}^{-1}$ is **not** orthogonal\n- $-P$ is orthogonal" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364116 1113 #uuid "5c887578-126d-5b52-8d2f-953ae4ec4272" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364116 1145 "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the product ${P}^{T}\\cdot ({P}^{T})^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\cdot ({P}^{T})^{T} & ={P}^{T}\\cdot P \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the product ${P}^{-1}\\cdot ({P}^{-1})^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{-1}\\cdot ({P}^{-1})^{T} & ={P}^{T}\\cdot ({P}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & ={P}^{T}P \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Computing the product $(-P)\\cdot (-P)^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-P)\\cdot (-P)^{T} & =(-P)\\cdot (-{P}^{T}) \\\\  & =P{P}^{T} \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364118 13194139535738 true] [17592186364117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364119 13194139535738 true] [17592186364117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364120 13194139535738 true] [17592186364117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364121 13194139535738 true] [17592186364117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364122 13194139535738 true] [17592186364117 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535738 true] [17592186364117 1041 "selection" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364117 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364118 13194139535738 true] [17592186364117 1110 #uuid "3f1fa5a6-a049-5168-9c25-a79ab0a25a51" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364118 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364118 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535738 true] [17592186364118 1111 #uuid "f63631da-fdb2-5e4d-8f2e-afdfc87f6e08" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364119 1034 "I only" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535738 true] [17592186364119 1111 #uuid "15a30673-26de-5e51-ae53-b8c8494b8c37" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364120 1034 "III only" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535738 true] [17592186364120 1111 #uuid "e4e90392-b3ee-58ce-9406-ad6c37206e9a" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364121 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364121 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535738 true] [17592186364121 1111 #uuid "98e88332-dd5a-5b90-85b8-2d9a3fd0fb72" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364122 1034 "II only" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535738 true] [17592186364122 1111 #uuid "f49139f9-6ba8-5b1c-ae96-5675525efbbc" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364123 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364124 13194139535738 true] [17592186364123 1089 "q-84352" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364123 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535738 true] [17592186364123 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the orthogonal matrix $Q?$\n\n- $5Q$ is also orthogonal\n- If $A=QB{Q}^{T}$ then $|det(A)|=|det(B)|$\n- ${Q}^{3}$ is the zero matrix" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364123 1113 #uuid "1bc22491-a63d-5614-9862-e7e8f8d05092" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364123 1145 "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the product $5Q\\cdot 5{Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5Q\\cdot (5Q)^{T} & =5Q\\cdot 5{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =25Q{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =25I \\\\  & \\ne I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing $|det(A)|,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(A)| & =|det(QB{Q}^{T})| \\\\  & =|det(Q)|\\cdot |det(B)|\\cdot |det({Q}^{T})| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |det(B)|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|det(B)|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Let's consider the identity matrix\n\n$$\nQ=I=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that $Q$ is an orthogonal matrix and also ${Q}^{3}=Q\\ne O.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535738 true] [17592186364124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364125 13194139535738 true] [17592186364124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364126 13194139535738 true] [17592186364124 1000 #edb/ref 